# ESLint Suppressions

When suppressing an ESLint rule, use the narrowest possible scope and always explain why.

## Rules

- Prefer `eslint-disable-next-line` over block-level `eslint-disable`; never file-level disables for a single offending line
- Name the specific rule being suppressed — a bare `// eslint-disable-next-line` silences everything on that line
- Add a short comment (same line or the line above) explaining **why** the suppression is legitimate
- If the same suppression keeps appearing, that's config pressure — fix it once in `eslint.config.mjs` instead of scattering disables

### Correct

```ts
const toProviderToolSet = (tools: Record<string, unknown>): ToolSet => {
  // eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/consistent-type-assertions -- The provider packages declare their tools against a different Tool type than the `ai` package.
  return tools as ToolSet;
};
```

The reason follows `--` on the same line: `eslint-comments/require-description`
refuses a suppression without one, and `eslint-comments/no-use` allows only
`eslint-disable-next-line`.

### Incorrect

```ts
/* eslint-disable */ // silences every rule for the rest of the file
return tools as ToolSet;
```
